          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In suitable “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate-free+spectrum"}> coordinate-free
            ” presentations of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
            (an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+ring"} A-infinity ring
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"}> E-infinity ring
            )) may be expressed directly as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
            on the indexing spaces, hence a functor that intertwines the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            of indexing spaces with that of the component spaces, but without explicitly mentioning the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
          %h3#general General
          %p
            So a
            %em functor with smash products
            is a suitably well behaved functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi Spaces
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E \;\colon\; \mathcal{D} \longrightarrow Spaces^{\ast/}
          %p
            from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{D},\wedge)
            to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+simplicial+sets"} pointed simplicial sets
            and equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{S}(V) \longrightarrow E(V)
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E(V) \wedge E(W) \longrightarrow E(V \wedge W)
          %p
            that are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associative
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unital
            in the evident sense.
          %h3#for_highly_structured_spectra For highly structured spectra
          %p
            For the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/highly+structured+spectra"} highly structured spectra
            such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-modules"} S-modules
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric smash product of spectra
            is due to
            %a{:href => "Day+convolution#DayMonoidsAreLaxMonoidalFunctorsOnTheSite"} this proposition
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#MMSS00"} MMSS 00, prop. 22.1, prop. 22.6
          %p
            (For instance accounts such as (
            %a{:href => "Adams+category#Kochmann96"}> Kochmann 96, section 3.3
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "orthogonal%20spectrum#Schwede14"} Schwede 14
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
            first as FSPs, before or introducing the smash product on spectra)
          %h3#for_excisive_functors For excisive functors
          %p
            For the monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure"} model structure
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excisive+functors"} excisive functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric smash product of spectra
            are equivalently FSPs is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#Lydakis98"}> Lydakis 98, remark 5.12
            ). See
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "model+structure+for+excisive+functors#MonoidsInLydakisModelStructureAreFSP"} this proposition
          %h2#ingredients Ingredients
          %h3#TopologicalEndsAndCoends Topological ends and coends
          %p
            For working with pointed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+functors"} topologically enriched functors
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            is particularly relevant: these are called (pointed topological enriched)
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ends"} ends
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coends"} coends
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coends"} coends
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalLeftKanExtensionBCoend"}
            below). Further below it is via left Kan extension along the ordinary smash product of pointed topological spaces (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"}> Day convolution
            ”) that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
            is induced.
